WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.560
My home is a small Inari shrine

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.940
that's been around since the Edo period.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.690
Our shrine is dedicated to the god 
of agriculture, Uka-no-Mitama.

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:15.650
See you around.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.870
Have a good day!

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.240
Good morning, Makoto-chan.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:19.990
Good morning!

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.620
Makoto-oneechan!

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:22.620
Good morning!

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.420
Good morning!

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.450
We wanted to make a wish to the 
fox before going to school!

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:30.090
Please help our recital go well!

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.260
It's a small shrine, so it's 
just my dad the priest, me...

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.270
And...

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.670
Hey.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.350
Gintaro-sama, the fox spirit who serves 
as the herald for this shrine.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.520
You're going to be late for school.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:52.790
What do I do?!

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.600
I'm gonna miss the bus again!

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.820
Oh, you haven't left yet, Makoto?!

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.530
Dad, take over!

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.110
Oh, are those oranges?

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:03.320
Yes, the fox spirit who 
lives here loves them.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.590
I'm leaving!

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.960
Does she have to make 
a scene every morning?

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.420
Gintaro is a herald, so ordinary 
people can't see him.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:27.470
The bus is here!

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.500
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.870
<b>Learning to Compromise</b>

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.870
I'm starving...

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.830
Um, it's first period.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:10.000
Are you serious?

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.540
Hey, Mako-chi...

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.040
Saeki, thanks for your help.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.670
Oh, Ikegami-san. I should thank you.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:19.760
Call me Yumi.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:21.300
Okay.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.260
But I'll never trust your fortunes.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.460
You made up with Shohei?

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:34.120
Yeah, all because Saeki used her 
fortune telling to help find a cat.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.520
Mako-chi, when did you become 
friends with Ikegami-san?

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.320
Um, it just kind of happened...

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.220
So Saeki was spot on!

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.510
I should ask her to tell my fortune!

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.040
No, no, no.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.380
I wouldn't recommend it.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.330
It was probably just a fluke.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.330
How's Mi-chan doing?

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.970
She's doing great!

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.290
Excuse me, that's enough chitchat.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.490
We're supposed to form teams 
so we can start playing.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.930
Six people to a team.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.910
Come on, we're on our own today.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.220
Don't be such a spoilsport, Funabashi.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.580
I might as well say this now.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.000
You're making life more 
difficult for everyone else

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.640
when you refuse to cooperate.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:15.960
What?

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.280
What brought this on?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.470
I'm not sure why you're 
trying to pick a fight.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:24.960
I'm not trying to pick a fight.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.790
I'm sure that a model student like 
you would think that we're useless.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:29.790
This doesn't look good.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:30.330
Yeah...

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:36.070
Well, you keep on trying to boss 
people around, Miss Vice President.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.240
So annoying.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.180
Let's go.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.840
Wait, Ikegami!

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.520
Honestly, she's a lost cause.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.030
Saeki-san.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.050
Um, yes?

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.220
I believe that you live in a shrine?

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.500
Yes...

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.290
You should choose your friends wisely.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.020
Huh?

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:57.770
Never mind.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:00.860
It's not my business if you 
want to be friends with her.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.310
However,

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.180
I hope that you'll stop distracting 
students with your fortune telling.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:10.530
I'm sure that you enjoy the 
attention you receive.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.200
What?

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.600
What?!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.460
Funabashi

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.850
I'm home, Mother.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.730
Welcome home, Hiwako-san.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:43.630
Is something wrong?

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.810
Um, where is Father?

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:51.040
His trip overseas has been extended, 
so he won't be back this week.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.160
I see...

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.610
Now hurry.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:56.910
Yes.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.380
So that's what happened.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.290
Are you listening to me, Gintaro?

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.750
Yeah...

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:04.870
Jeez...

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.290
As I was saying, Gintaro,

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:10.590
Funabashi-san comes from 
a tea ceremony family.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.070
Her father is a member of the Diet,

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.470
and she's Vice President 
of the student council.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:18.390
She's smart and pretty,

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.130
but she can be difficult.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:22.930
Are you listening?

00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.120
Yeah...

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:29.230
I mean, compared to Funabashi-san, 
I may look like a total failure,

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:32.150
but that doesn't mean 
she has to be so mean.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:33.450
Plus, she gave Yumi-chan a hard time.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.640
Well, I shouldn't let it get to me.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.840
I just have to get my act together

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.770
so Funabashi-san stops 
saying those things.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:44.500
Okay! I have to work harder, yep!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.970
Hypocrite.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.970
What?!

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.740
Aren't you mad about 
what that girl said?

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.640
Cut the goody two-shoes 
act and vent away.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:58.520
I'm not...

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:02.240
Seriously, humans care too much 
about what other people think.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:04.730
You're always complaining 
to me when you're home.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.020
Huh?

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:09.190
That other girl sounds 
more reasonable to me.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.020
You're wrong.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:13.410
I'm not that bad...

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.470
Besides, we'd have a huge 
mess if everyone did

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.090
whatever they wanted!

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.740
Not my problem if humans 
want to make a huge mess.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:23.280
I'm home!

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:24.710
Welcome home, Dad.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:26.920
It's really hot out there today.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.490
In that respect,
 Tatsuo is really something.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:33.620
There haven't been many 
priests like him.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.510
What? Is Dad really special?

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:39.480
Yeah, I never know what he's thinking.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:40.200
Huh?

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:41.810
Oh, what's going on?

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.960
What did Gintaro-sama say?

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.960
It sounds like my father's 
trip has been extended.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.220
Yes.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.920
It'll be a few more days 
before he returns.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:14.470
Good morning!

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.570
Hey, Saeki!

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.970
Oh, Yumi-chan. Good morning.

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:25.740
Have a good day, Hiwako-sama.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.550
Yeah, she's living the good life.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:35.250
No wonder she's a snob.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.220
Sure, we were fooling around,

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.540
but that doesn't mean she 
should unload on us.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.450
Now, now... Can't we all get along?

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.860
Are you crazy?

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:46.410
I want nothing to do with her.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:48.790
Though I might change my 
mind if she apologizes.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.120
Ah, Yumi-chan!

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.280
U-Um... Good morning, Funabashi-san.

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:57.890
Good morning.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.100
Say, Funabashi-san...

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:04.800
Would you be willing to 
apologize to Yumi-chan?

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:07.350
Why should I? 
Did I say something wrong?

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.040
But—

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:14.280
I'll admit that I put her in 
an uncomfortable situation,

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:18.490
but that's necessary in a group 
environment like a school.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:21.570
We're in high school.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:24.540
We're not allowed to live as we please.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:26.420
Huh?

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.950
The bell's about to ring.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.230
That comedian's really funny.

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:39.420
I saw that segment!

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.780
He was hilarious!

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.910
He'll be ancient history in a year, though.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:43.970
No way!

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.560
Hey, Funabashi.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.520
Yes.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.940
Class 6 is the only one that 
hasn't turned in their reports.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:50.930
I asked you to collect those, right?

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:51.780
Huh?

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:53.230
You're usually on top of things.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.540
Bring them to the office right away.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:56.120
Right.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.270
Huh?

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.400
Serves her right.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:07.160
Ishii-san, you said you would 
drop off the reports for me.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:10.250
What? When'd I say that?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.740
Don't blame other people 
when you screw up.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.270
Stop playing dumb.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:14.960
You agreed to take them.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.970
What? No way.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:20.930
Funabashi.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:22.760
We'll drop these off for you.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.410
You look busy.

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:26.430
Thanks, I appreciate it.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:29.520
Stop fooling around and 
hand the reports over!

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.860
No idea what you're talking about. 
Why don't you look around?

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:33.490
Um, I saw—

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:36.260
Saeki-san, you should stay out of this.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:37.070
But...

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:39.630
Those girls are friends 
with Ikegami-san.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.360
Yeah, they're scary.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.030
It's out of our hands.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:53.960
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.730
Makoto, you're late today.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:07.180
Hey, now. Why are you trying 
to run into the statue?

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:11.650
What's wrong? Why the long face?

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:13.460
Say, Gin...

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.870
Am I a hypocrite?

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:23.530
I would like Yumi-chan, Funabashi-san,

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.240
and everyone to just get along.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:30.250
But deep down, I don't 
really care what they do,

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:33.540
as long as I'm not involved.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:38.550
Sorry about making you listen 
to me complain again, Gintaro.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:42.520
Stupid. Just let it all out.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:47.280
You usually tend to speak your mind,

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:51.390
but since you can see me,
 you never get to actually vent.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:55.140
Just let it all out and 
you'll feel better.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:57.400
That's what a shrine is for.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.650
But you don't like to 
listen to me complain.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:02.990
You see...

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:07.280
I'll just pretend that 
I never heard a word.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:18.420
<b>Student Council</b>

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:18.420
Kirishima-senpai, here is the budget 
plan for the student council.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:20.360
You move fast.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.630
Anyway, let's go out somewhere 
after we're finished.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:26.300
I'll be leaving now.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.230
She's so shy.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.630
Saeki!

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:41.830
Oh, Yumi-chan.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.120
It's a good thing you're still around.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.440
Can I stay at your place tonight?

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:47.830
Huh? At my place?

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:50.080
I got in a fight with my parents.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.710
I asked around but 
didn't have any luck.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.130
Oh, sure, I guess...

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:59.090
Super! I'll go grab my bag!

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.340
Wait, Yumi-chan.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:01.720
I need to go to the restroom.

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:02.680
Okay.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:08.970
<b>Girls' Restroom</b>

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.910
Well, I guess this works out.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.970
I'll have time to talk to her 
about Funabashi-san tonight.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.390
Oh, it's Saeki.

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.840
Why weren't you watching the entrance?

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:17.980
Well...

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:19.690
Funabashi-san.

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:25.330
Saeki-san, we're busy right now.

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.600
Can you go somewhere else?

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:29.240
Why are you taking the lead?

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.320
Do you understand the situation here?

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.480
Your business is with me, 
not with Saeki-san.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.780
I'm willing to listen to 
what you have to say,

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:40.420
but this isn't the place—

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.810
I can't stand that attitude of yours!

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:46.590
What does Kirishima-senpai 
see in this girl?!

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:50.120
Huh? What does the student council 
president have to do with this?

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:50.120
Um, can you stop this?

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.290
None of your business.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:51.920
U-Um...

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.640
Shut up, Saeki!

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:54.460
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:55.640
<i>Th-They're scary...</i>

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:03.130
What are you doing?

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:04.810
Yumi-chan.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.320
I-Ikegami...

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:13.960
What's this? Are you teaching 
Funabashi a lesson?

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.250
Why's Saeki here?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.370
Oh, remember how mad you were at Saeki?

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.500
So we figured we'd—

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.460
Saeki just happened to walk in.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:22.560
What?

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.950
I'm the one who doesn't like Funabashi.

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:26.630
What does that have to 
do with all of you?

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.230
W-Well...

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:32.180
Can you stay out of my problems?

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:35.900
Besides, the teachers are coming.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.790
Everyone can hear you outside.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:39.210
Crap!

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:46.920
Huh? I thought you were friends 
with them, Yumi-chan.

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.000
What?

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:51.420
We talk and stuff, 
but we're not really friends.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:52.070
Huh?

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:54.540
What is it?

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.680
Nothing!

00:14:56.680 --> 00:15:00.210
<i>Yumi-chan isn't who she seems to be.</i>

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:01.960
So why—

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.210
Should I thank you?

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:06.340
I don't really care,

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.670
since you still tick me off.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.520
I don't intend to apologize.

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:15.890
Do you understand that you're 
making trouble for other people?

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:17.630
I don't see a problem!

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:20.310
You may be smart, 
but I wouldn't want to be you!

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.500
Yumi-chan!

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.400
Doesn't she piss you off?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.360
She's so judgmental.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:27.970
Judgmental?

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:31.320
You're the one who's being judgmental!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.240
I'm a good student?

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:35.830
My parents are elite?

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.240
I'm usually on top of things?!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.500
"My daughter should be 
able to do everything?!"

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:41.730
I've had enough!

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.310
I am what I am!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.710
Don't try to make me something I'm not!

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:52.550
O-Oh no!

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.750
S-Sorry, I didn't mean 
to lose control.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:59.470
Man, what was that about?

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.190
That threw me off.

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:05.090
You usually play it cool 
and show no emotion,

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:07.190
but you're just like the rest of us.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:08.970
Don't hold it all in.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:12.660
I bet you were just jealous of me.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.110
I'm not jealous!

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:17.790
Looks like I'm right.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:18.920
Now, now...

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.600
Say, Funabashi-san,

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:23.590
Yumi-chan's staying 
at my place tonight.

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:25.590
Would you like to join us?

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:26.310
Hey, Saeki!

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:27.800
At your place?

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:31.470
I live in a shrine, 
but it's nothing special.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:35.020
Still, I was thinking it'd 
be a new experience.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:36.760
Is it okay, Yumi-chan?

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:38.970
I guess it's okay.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:43.140
S-Sorry, Yumi-chan.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:44.160
I'm sorry.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:47.190
Why are you crying?

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.500
I'm sorry...

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.140
<i>Gintaro, I'm such a fool.</i>

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:00.610
Welcome back.

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:03.000
Yoshizumi, take this 
message to my mother.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:05.370
"I won't be coming home tonight."

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.620
Let's go, then.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.280
Did you see the look on his face?!

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:15.090
Was that the right thing to say?

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.300
I've always wanted to say that.

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:30.780
That's our shrine.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:36.360
Welcome back, Makoto-chan.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.150
I'm back, Granny!

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:42.860
I made lots of pickled vegetables, 
so I brought some over.

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:44.990
Thank you for being so good to us!

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:46.920
Hey, there.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.180
You're not supposed to use 
the middle of the stairs.

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:50.750
Huh? Why not?

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:54.890
The middle of the path is 
reserved for the gods.

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:57.110
So you're not supposed to walk there.

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:59.590
Oh, I never knew about that custom.

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:01.550
I think I've heard about it.

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:03.350
That's right,

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:08.090
but sometimes I forget 
and walk in the middle.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:23.890
It's so quiet...

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:27.250
My house is quiet, 
but in a different way.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.650
For some reason, 
this place is very calming.

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:33.810
Yep.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.090
Welcome home, Makoto.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.210
Oh? Are these your friends?

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:40.920
Wait, Dad! Why are you 
dressed like that?!

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:43.350
Hello.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:45.120
Hi there.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.380
Hello.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:49.020
Um, we were just told

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:53.020
that the middle of the path 
is reserved for the gods...

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:54.340
That's right.

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.320
Once you pass under the gate, 
you're on sacred ground.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:01.200
When visiting a shrine, 
you're supposed to walk on the left side

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.450
and leave room for the gods.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:06.450
At the same time,

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:11.540
it also ensures that people 
don't run into each other.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:14.460
It was a way of teaching 
the lesson that people

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.860
should learn to compromise.

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:21.180
Learn to compromise...

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:25.210
But our herald always says

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:29.550
that people should just 
run into each other.

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:32.040
Herald?

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:33.790
A herald is a messenger of the gods.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.260
Ours is a fox spirit.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:36.840
I wouldn't worry too much about it.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:39.270
Oh, Dad?

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.800
Can they stay here tonight?

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:43.120
Sure, that's fine.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.140
Thanks, Mr. Saeki!

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.240
Thank you for your hospitality.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.790
No need for that. 
We're glad to have you.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.210
Go ahead and make yourself at home.

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.550
Okay!

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:55.520
Are you going to take over 
this shrine, Saeki-san?

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:02.800
I'm not sure yet.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.680
Are you going to take over your 
family's tea ceremony school?

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.800
I don't know.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:12.350
To be honest, I'm not sure 
what I want to do.

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:16.210
Shrines are magical places.

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:19.540
They bring all kinds 
of people together.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:21.340
Together?

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:22.270
Uh-huh.

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:25.060
This shrine has brought three 
different people together.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:30.120
I don't want to lose that magic.

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:37.690
You know, I want to become a vet,

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:40.770
but it's impossible with my grades,

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:42.550
so I'm exploring my other options.

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:45.150
Huh? You're giving up?

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:49.020
They say that you should find 
something you want to do,

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:52.960
but there's no guarantee that you'll 
 actually achieve that dream.

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:56.540
I can help you study.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.030
For real?

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:00.800
You're pretty nice.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:04.500
Oh? That means you thought 
I was a bad person.

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:06.920
You're gonna hold that against me, huh?

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:08.210
I wouldn't say that.

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.580
I can already see where this is going.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:10.930
That's not true.

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:13.990
Oh, does that look on your face tell 
me that everything's resolved?

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:15.290
Uh-huh.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:19.720
Don't you wish you were 
born to a family

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:21.300
where you could do 
whatever you wanted?

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:23.340
I can see you.

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:24.760
What more could I ask for?

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:32.930
I took a quick peek.

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:37.350
It looks like the three of you 
will be together for a long time.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:40.640
Not that you would care about how 
compatible you are with girls.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:45.000
Gintaro.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.030
What is it?

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:47.610
Thanks.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:49.100
I love you.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.060
Did you say something?

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:53.160
Nope.

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:56.040
Bah, she got me.

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:02.530
After ringing the bell, 
you pay your respects twice

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:08.230
clap twice,

00:22:13.030 --> 00:22:14.230
and pay your respects one more time.

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:20.610
Hey, I can actually see our fox spirit.

00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:24.440
Whoa, this girl's got 
a few screws loose.

00:22:24.440 --> 00:22:26.020
I believe you.

00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:28.660
What?! What's wrong with you?

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:32.540
I mean, I could totally 
see one living here.

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:19.970
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:19.970
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:24:10.920 --> 00:24:16.110
The center of the path at a 
shrine is reserved for the gods.

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:17.510
When visiting a shrine,

00:24:17.510 --> 00:24:19.100
you should avoid walking 
 down the middle of the path.

00:24:19.620 --> 00:24:22.120
Next time: "The Place Where the Gods Are."

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:25.000
<b>The Place Where the Gods Are</b>

00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:25.000
May fortune be with you.
